                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:9",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moroni also sent unto him, desiring him that he would be faithful in maintaining that quarter of the land, and that he would seek every opportunity to scourge the Lamanites in that quarter, as much as was in his power, that perhaps he might take again by stratagem or some other way those cities which had been taken out of their hands; and that he also would fortify and strengthen the cities round about, which had not fallen into the hands of the Lamanites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Trustworthiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Trustworthiness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Trustworthiness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Trustworthiness",
                "entryId": "tg-trustworthiness",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:10",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And he also said unto him, I would come unto you, but behold, the Lamanites are upon us in the borders of the land by the west sea; and behold, I go against them, therefore I cannot come unto you.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:11",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Now, the king (Ammoron) had departed out of the land of Zarahemla, and had made known unto the queen concerning the death of his brother, and had gathered together a large number of men, and had marched forth against the Nephites on the borders by the west sea.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Alma 51:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 51:28.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 51:28",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 51,
                    "end": 51,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 28,
                        "end": 28
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:12",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus he was endeavoring to harass the Nephites, and to draw away a part of their forces to that part of the land, while he had commanded those whom he had left to possess the cities which he had taken, that they should also harass the Nephites on the borders by the east sea, and should take possession of their lands as much as it was in their power, according to the power of their armies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:13",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus were the Nephites in those dangerous circumstances in the ending of the twenty and sixth year of the reign of the judges over the people of Nephi.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:14",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "But behold, it came to pass in the twenty and seventh year of the reign of the judges, that Teancum, by the command of Moroni—who had established armies to protect the south and the west borders of the land, and had begun his march towards the land Bountiful, that he might assist Teancum with his men in retaking the cities which they had lost—",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:15",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Teancum had received orders to make an attack upon the city of Mulek, and retake it if it were possible.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:16",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Teancum made preparations to make an attack upon the city of Mulek, and march forth with his army against the Lamanites; but he saw that it was impossible that he could overpower them while they were in their fortifications; therefore he abandoned his designs and returned again to the city Bountiful, to wait for the coming of Moroni, that he might receive strength to his army.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:17",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Moroni did arrive with his army at the land of Bountiful, in the latter end of the twenty and seventh year of the reign of the judges over the people of Nephi.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:18",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And in the commencement of the twenty and eighth year, Moroni and Teancum and many of the chief captains held a council of war—what they should do to cause the Lamanites to come out against them to battle; or that they might by some means flatter them out of their strongholds, that they might gain advantage over them and take again the city of Mulek.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "Alma 49:5; 55:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 49:5; 55:23.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 49:5; 55:23",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 49,
                    "end": 49,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 5,
                        "end": 5
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "start": 55,
                    "end": 55,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 23,
                        "end": 23
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:19",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass they sent embassies to the army of the Lamanites, which protected the city of Mulek, to their leader, whose name was Jacob, desiring him that he would come out with his armies to meet them upon the plains between the two cities. But behold, Jacob, who was a Zoramite, would not come out with his army to meet them upon the plains.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 278,
            "end": 286,
            "text": "Alma 48:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 48:5.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 48:5",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 48,
                    "end": 48,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 5,
                        "end": 5
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:20",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Moroni, having no hopes of meeting them upon fair grounds, therefore, he resolved upon a plan that he might decoy the Lamanites out of their strongholds.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 133,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "Josh. 8:13; Alma 43:31 (30–43); 56:30."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:21",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore he caused that Teancum should take a small number of men and march down near the seashore; and Moroni and his army, by night, marched in the wilderness, on the west of the city Mulek; and thus, on the morrow, when the guards of the Lamanites had discovered Teancum, they ran and told it unto Jacob, their leader.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 187,
            "end": 192,
            "text": "Alma 51:26; 53:6 (2, 6)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:22",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the armies of the Lamanites did march forth against Teancum, supposing by their numbers to overpower Teancum because of the smallness of his numbers. And as Teancum saw the armies of the Lamanites coming out against him he began to retreat down by the seashore, northward.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:23",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that when the Lamanites saw that he began to flee, they took courage and pursued them with vigor. And while Teancum was thus leading away the Lamanites who were pursuing them in vain, behold, Moroni commanded that a part of his army who were with him should march forth into the city, and take possession of it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:24",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus they did, and slew all those who had been left to protect the city, yea, all those who would not yield up their weapons of war.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "Alma 44:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 44:6.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 44:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 44,
                    "end": 44,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 6,
                        "end": 6
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:25",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus Moroni had obtained possession of the city Mulek with a part of his army, while he marched with the remainder to meet the Lamanites when they should return from the pursuit of Teancum.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:26",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the Lamanites did pursue Teancum until they came near the city Bountiful, and then they were met by Lehi and a small army, which had been left to protect the city Bountiful.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:27",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "And now behold, when the chief captains of the Lamanites had beheld Lehi with his army coming against them, they fled in much confusion, lest perhaps they should not obtain the city Mulek before Lehi should overtake them; for they were wearied because of their march, and the men of Lehi were fresh.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:28",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Now the Lamanites did not know that Moroni had been in their rear with his army; and all they feared was Lehi and his men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:29",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "Now Lehi was not desirous to overtake them till they should meet Moroni and his army.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:30",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that before the Lamanites had retreated far they were surrounded by the Nephites, by the men of Moroni on one hand, and the men of Lehi on the other, all of whom were fresh and full of strength; but the Lamanites were wearied because of their long march.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:31",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moroni commanded his men that they should fall upon them until they had given up their weapons of war.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 52:32",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 52,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Jacob, being their leader, being also a Zoramite, and having an unconquerable spirit, he led the Lamanites forth to battle with exceeding fury against Moroni.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "Alma 30:59."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 30:59.",
